  "notes": "Swedish disco-house/dance-pop revivalists. `confidence` is low because the research rates the entry medium-low — \"era and idiom documented; parameters are disco-house convention and marked\". The one harmonic claim it does make is the differentiator: \"the disco revival means the harmony carries more motion than Eurodance's static vamps\", with \"minor-key disco vamps with 7ths and a bright chorus lift\" `[LOW-CONF]`, repeated here. So `extensions` inverts the lane's triad default to 0.32/0.48/0.20 and the harmonic rhythm drops `vamp` entirely. The kit is the entry's own: \"four-square kick, clap on 2&4, disco offbeat hats opening to 16ths, plus cowbell and tambourine; string and horn stabs land on the backbeat\", which is a cowbell/tambourine/conga bed on the offbeat at 4-7 hits a bar and a 16th-weighted hat. The bass is called \"the second hook — moving in 16ths against the kick\", so it is an independent riff at 0.6 roots with a high anticipation and four passing tones. ⚠ Every velocity, density and probability above is INFERRED.",
